        "number": 4791,
        "title": "Add app:// as a valid request origin protocol",
        "body": "I am trying to query my local instance of Ollama from Obsidian, which according to dev tools has the origin app://obsidian.md. Wireshark says this traffic ends up going out over 127.0.0.1, so I suspect that app:// is just not a supported protocol. I tried adding \"app://obsidian.md\" to the OLLAMA_ORIGINS env variable but was getting errors about it not being a valid origin. \r\n\r\nIt seems like there is a lot of support beyond http including chrome-extension, so seeing app supported would easily fix my issue and probably has common applications beyond working with Obsidian.",
        "comments": []
    },
